        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nThis design was transferred onto canvas by a specialist craftsman known as a pattern drawer. He modified biblical scenes published in Antwerp in 1585 for the outlines of the two main groups of figures (see photograph). He then probably used English prints as the source for the animals, birds, insects and flowers in the background. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
